# Compiled Compact output is committed so a judge can reproduce it from source
# (see .gitignore and docs/ROADMAP.md). The compiler emits LF; core.autocrlf on
# Windows would otherwise rewrite these on checkout, so a clone made on Windows
# and a clone made on Linux would not hold the same bytes — and the
# "recompile and compare" check would fail for reasons that have nothing to do
# with the contract. Pin them to LF and treat the binary ones as binary.
contracts/**/managed/**/contract/*.js      text eol=lf
contracts/**/managed/**/contract/*.js.map  text eol=lf
contracts/**/managed/**/contract/*.d.ts    text eol=lf
contracts/**/managed/**/compiler/*.json    text eol=lf
contracts/**/managed/**/zkir/*.zkir        text eol=lf
contracts/**/managed/**/zkir/*.bzkir       binary

# The .compact source itself is the input to that check.
*.compact                                   text eol=lf
